2. Cloud Engine definition

"Cloud Engine" means either:
(a) an Internet Computer subnet or execution environment offered, designated,
marketed or operated as a Cloud Engine, including through Open Cloud; or
(b) an equivalent private, sovereign, dedicated or permissioned subnet or
execution environment running the Internet Computer Protocol or a fork or
adaptation of it, whose capacity or node set is reserved for, selected by, or
controlled by a customer, tenant, enterprise or affiliated group rather than
operated as an ordinary shared public Internet Computer subnet.

This definition applies regardless of branding, provider, owner, hosting
location, payment method, profit, connection to mainnet or governance mechanism.
It includes self-hosted and third-party-hosted environments and renamed or
modified implementations. Ordinary shared public Internet Computer subnets are
not Cloud Engines merely because individual canisters have private data or
controllers. An isolated local development replica or simulator used solely for
development or testing, with no operational workloads or service to third
parties, is not a Cloud Engine. Testing on an actual Cloud Engine is not exempt.

3. No Cloud Engine use

You must not deploy, install, execute or otherwise use the Software, in whole
or in part, on a Cloud Engine. You must not use the Software from another
environment to provision, deploy to, administer, operate, or provide relay or
other runtime services for a Cloud Engine or workloads running on one.

You must not cause, authorize or knowingly facilitate those prohibited uses
through a contractor, affiliate, intermediary, hosted service, wrapper, proxy
or modified version. Splitting components across environments, changing names,
removing checks, or modifying the Software does not remove this condition.
Burning ICP or cycles, including burning 100%, creates no exception.

This section is an express condition of every permission granted by this
license. No permission for a prohibited use is granted. There is no automatic
conversion to an unrestricted license after a period of time.

